Report read errors in comm.
A read error ends the line reader's input just as end of file does, and
comm never checked the streams' error flags, so it compared what had
been read and exited 0, listing the rest of the other file as unique to
it. After the last line is written, die with the file name if either
input had a read error.

---
 coreutils/comm.c |    3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/coreutils/comm.c
+++ b/coreutils/comm.c
@@ -108,6 +108,9 @@
 		}
 	}
 
+	die_if_ferror(stream[0], argv[0]);
+	die_if_ferror(stream[1], argv[1]);
+
 	if (ENABLE_FEATURE_CLEAN_UP) {
 		fclose(stream[0]);
 		fclose(stream[1]);
